WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:02.283
- All right, here we go.

00:00:03.866 --> 00:00:08.750
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:09.800
Wow, okay.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.874
I've got tears in my eyes.

00:00:11.874 --> 00:00:15.207
(upbeat rhythmic music)

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.040
You drive-through,
almost as if you're going

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.092
to a McDonald's or a Starbucks.

00:00:22.092 --> 00:00:23.090
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.720
I'm supposed to fill
out this questionnaire

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.810
so that the health officials ahead of us

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.610
can identify whether or not
I'm gonna need some testing.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.848
They are taking my temperature,
from both ears actually.

00:00:35.848 --> 00:00:37.990
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.910
They've just shown me
that my body temperature

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:43.073
is 36.6 degrees Celsius.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:46.098
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:46.098 --> 00:00:46.931
Ah.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.223
It's very ticklish and a bit abrupt.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.380
In a day or two, I will
probably receive my results.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.991
I will probably get them
through text messages.

00:01:06.991 --> 00:01:10.574
(cheerful xylophone music)

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.930
South Korea has seen cases
rise more than 200-fold

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.630
in just a few weeks.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.730
And a lot of that could be because testing

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.230
is so widespread here.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.490
The government has set up more than 500

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:26.980
coronavirus testing sites,
processing more than

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:30.740
210,000 people in a few weeks.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.010
Some critics say that
if the government had,

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.660
early on, closed its border with China

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.640
and restricted travel from the epicenter

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.100
of the country's epidemic, than maybe

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.950
it wouldn't have needed to
create so many testing sites,

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.510
like this drive-through.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:57.257
- This meant that COVID-19
can be characterized

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.474
as a pandemic.

00:01:59.474 --> 00:02:02.891
(bright xylophone music)

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.120
- [Andrew] The biggest takeaway is that

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.280
the drive-through testing site is quick,

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.930
efficient and minimizes the risk

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.590
that potential patients
might get the virus

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.430
from those who already have it.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:20.020
The biggest limitation though,
is you must be able to drive

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:23.560
and have access to a car
to use this facility.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.090
This probably means people who can't drive

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:28.700
or people with disabilities
will face difficulty

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.943
in coming here and undertaking the test.

